  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel space with its canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero and all approved ambient instances. Let W:E->R be C1 and assume exp(-W) is integrable against volume. Define mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), the actual normalized Gibbs measure exp(-W)/integral exp(-W) times volume. In this full-space setting the approved context gives the positive normalized density; no separate positive-partition hypothesis is a displayed binder in this statement.\nFor every real-linear partial operator D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E), assume D is closable and its graph is characterized exactly as follows: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H, (a,H) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real function phi:E->R with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) mu-almost everywhere. D.closure is the genuine single-valued operator from that same graph closure, with its actual submodule domain.\nThen for every u in this SAME D.closure.domain, if D.closure(u)=0 as an actual vector L2(mu) class, there exists a real c with (u as a scalar L2(mu) representative)(x)=c for mu-almost every x.\nD is fixed before every u. The constant c is selected after u and may depend on u; no universal common constant for all zero-output elements is claimed. The premise is equality of the true closed-gradient output to the zero vector quotient, not a claim that the rough representative's totalized derivative vanishes pointwise. C1 regularity of W suffices here and no curvature, positive spectral gap, dense-domain condition or mean-zero assumption is added. This is a universal implication for a supplied closable exact-gradient D, not an existential construction of D. It is one direction only: zero output implies weighted-AE constancy. It does not produce constant-function domain membership or prove full kernel equality, nor a centered/epsilon-zero/range/Poincare or further inequality/core/composition theorem. There is no joint measurable choice of constants.",
    "text_sha256": "e5e794883ab6a7001ca047ef6a582315173e94fde1077a76316b98b1baa3ff60",
    "decoder": "anonymous_decoder_20261006",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "25e142d4cfc201bec0809181a06dd5b629b3b9b08e4382d7c73ac6e0b184a6c8",
